":"Ring-theoretic properties of the completed surface-cone candidate","statements":["SurfaceConeCandidateSupport"]}],"scope":"The small Cohen–Macaulay module conjecture asks whether every complete local domain has a nonzero finitely generated maximal Cohen–Macaulay module. The linked formalization verifies only the ring-theoretic candidate: there exists a three-dimensional complete Noetherian integrally closed local domain over $\\mathbb C$ whose residue field is $\\mathbb C$.\n\nIt does not prove that this ring lacks a nonzero finitely generated maximal Cohen–Macaulay module, or the paper's counterexample essentially of finite type.","title":"A counterexample to the small Cohen–Macaulay module conjecture","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/docs/195.md"}},"provenance":{"kind":"computed-navigation","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","rule":"Projection of the pinned ledger; no new mathematical assessment."},"reader_comparison":{"headline_coverage":"agree","method":"Compare reported scope categories; notes remain attributed and are not adjudicated.","points":[{"definitions_to_check":null,"gap":"The counterexample itself (no nonzero finitely generated MCM module) and the essentially-of-finite-type example are not stated; only properties of the candidate ring are, and those properties are existential.","note":null,"reading":"reading:2332a680c9a422722b667e83","source_term":"SUPPORT-ONLY","state":"supporting"},{"definitions_to_check":"candidate_ring_properties (the statement itself): a bare existence claim over an unconstrained R; it is not tied to the paper's completed section ring R(X,H) (the proof uses ExplicitCone.completedRing, the statement does not mention it) and is satisfied by the regular ring C[[x,y,z]]; the key property (no nonzero finitely generated module of depth three) is absent. ; IsIntegrallyClosed R: R is integrally closed in its fraction field (normal domain); standard. ; IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) R: R is Hausdorff and complete for the maximal-ideal-adic topology; standard. ; ringKrullDim R = 3: Krull dimension 3 (value in WithBot N-infinity); standard. ; Function.Bijective (algebraMap C (IsLocalRing.ResidueField R)): the structure map C -> R/m is bijective, i.e. residue field C; standard. ; Algebra C R: the paper's 'containing C' is encoded as an algebra structure over C; standard.","gap":null,"note":"Lean states only that some C-algebra R is a three-dimensional, m-adically complete, Noetherian, integrally closed local domain with residue field C; it never mentions modules, depth or Cohen-Macaulayness, so the defining property of the headline (no nonzero finitely generated module of depth 3) and the essentially-finite-type corollary are not stated. As typed the existential is also satisfied by C[[x,y,z]] and does not name the surface cone, so it records only the ring-theoretic half of the construction.","reading":"reading:c243110a57899825e62f1d53","source_term":"supporting-only","state":"supporting"}],"readings":["reading:2332a680c9a422722b667e83","reading:c243110a57899825e62f1d53"],"state":"agree"},"readings":[{"availability":"recorded","credit":{"atlas_pin":"755c4b729512c7e2c7d1d3303eb9706f5adf1681","authors":[{"handle":"carlostoledo1891","name":"Carlos Toledo"}],"kind":"third-party-reported","license":"MIT","method":"Every Comparator challenge re-run on Linux with nanoda switched on, decided by a preregistered rule; every family's challenge statements read against OpenAI's headline, clause by clause. Decider: Comparator (leanprover/comparator d03acab1 = tag v4.34.0, built with the release's toolchain v4.34.1), lean4export 076e8e57, landrun 811cfff5, nanoda_lib 3a240721 — on GitHub's Linux runners (.github/workflows/openai-math-kernel.yml), one j","name":"Carlos Toledo, cert-machine","pin":"9814e4c06281e34a113ce853d7d99ccce160b750","repository":"https://github.com/carlostoledo1891/